# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redis Detective — example environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env` or a GitHub App private key.
# The CLI loads `.env` automatically from the current directory or a parent;
# variables already set in the shell take precedence. Node does not do this
# on its own.
#
# The `redis-detective` CLI health check / diagnosis needs NOTHING from this
# file except optionally REDIS_URL. No signup, no GitHub, no LLM key required.
# GitHub vars are only for the optional second-pass candidate commits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- CLI (read-only) -------------------------------------------------------
# Default target for `redis-detective` when --url is not passed.
# The CLI issues read-only commands (INFO, SCAN, TYPE, PTTL, MEMORY USAGE on
# sampled keys only). Prefer a replica or a user with a read-only ACL.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- Optional: candidate commits -------------------------------------------
# Preferred: GitHub App (org). Solo fallback: `gh auth login` (no env needed),
# or set GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN. App env wins when complete — see ADR 0002.
#
# Used with `--snapshots` + `--repo owner/repo` (second pass; reuse the same
# snapshot directory). Or, during `--snapshots`, when GITHUB_REPOSITORY is set
# *and* a credential signal is present (GITHUB_APP_ID and/or GITHUB_TOKEN /
# GH_TOKEN) — so a GitHub Actions checkout does not silently opt a Redis-only
# diagnosis into GitHub auth. Note: default Actions GITHUB_TOKEN often needs
# contents: read (and pull-requests: read) on the job to list commits/PRs.
#
# --- GitHub App (preferred) ---
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
# Either an absolute path to the .pem file, or the base64-encoded key contents.
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_BASE64=
# Repository to search for candidate commits, as "owner/repo" (CI fallback).
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=
# --- Personal token (only when App env is incomplete) ---
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GH_TOKEN=

# --- Optional: explanation wording (packages/reasoner) ---------------------
# The reasoner is the ONLY package permitted to call an LLM, and only to put an
# already-computed EvidenceGraph into words. See packages/reasoner/AGENTS.md.
# Optional. When unset, the CLI uses the deterministic template explanation.
LLM_PROVIDER=
LLM_MODEL=
LLM_API_KEY=
# OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions root, including /v1. Defaults to https://api.openai.com/v1.
LLM_BASE_URL=
